  "concept": "Always settle the closest unsettled node; valid when no edge has negative weight.",
  "prompt": "The graph maps each node to a list of <code>(neighbour, weight)</code> pairs with weights &ge; 0. Write <code>dijkstra(graph, start)</code> returning <code>{node: shortest distance from start}</code> for every reachable node. Use <code>heapq</code> for the priority queue.",
  "fn": "dijkstra",
  "starter": "import heapq\n\ndef dijkstra(graph, start):\n    dist = {}\n    heap = [(0, start)]\n    # TODO: pop the smallest (d, node); skip it if already settled; settle it; push its neighbours with d + weight.\n    return dist\n",
  "solution": "import heapq\n\ndef dijkstra(graph, start):\n    dist = {}\n    heap = [(0, start)]\n    while heap:\n        d, node = heapq.heappop(heap)\n        if node in dist:\n            continue\n        dist[node] = d\n        for nxt, w in graph.get(node, []):\n            if nxt not in dist:\n                heapq.heappush(heap, (d + w, nxt))\n    return dist\n",
  "test": "import random\nrnd = random.Random(2)\ng = {\"A\": [(\"B\", 1), (\"C\", 4)], \"B\": [(\"C\", 2), (\"D\", 6)], \"C\": [(\"D\", 3)], \"D\": []}\nassert dijkstra(g, \"A\") == {\"A\": 0, \"B\": 1, \"C\": 3, \"D\": 6}\nassert dijkstra({\"s\": []}, \"s\") == {\"s\": 0}\nfor _ in range(250):\n    n = rnd.randint(1, 8)\n    graph = {i: [(j, rnd.randint(0, 9)) for j in range(n) if j != i and rnd.random() < 0.3] for i in range(n)}\n    INF = float(\"inf\"); ref = {i: INF for i in range(n)}; ref[0] = 0\n    for _ in range(n):                                  # Bellman-Ford as an independent reference\n        for u in graph:\n            for v, w in graph[u]:\n                if ref[u] + w < ref[v]:\n                    ref[v] = ref[u] + w\n    expected = {k: v for k, v in ref.items() if v < INF}\n    assert dijkstra(graph, 0) == expected, f\"wrong distances for {graph}: got {dijkstra(graph, 0)}, expected {expected}\"\n",
  "hints": [
   "heapq.heappush(heap, (distance, node)) keeps the smallest distance on top.",
   "The same node may be pushed several times; ignore a popped node that is already in dist."
  ],
